id: pm-vcs-phase6stage
title: Stream ordinary large-file staging into native CDC manifests
description: "Connect vcs add to bounded CDC for non-record regular files at least 1 MiB, preserve FileIds across moves and PM attribution, keep status bounded for manifest-backed files, and publish reproducible scale and GC byte receipts."
type: Feature
pm_format_version: 2
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-10-21T14:41:01.521Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-21T15:50:36.697Z"
author: codex-agent
acceptance_criteria: Native add and status handle large binary files without whole-file buffers; rename plus edit retains FileId and PM change trace; compression-independent identities and range verification pass; GC reports physical candidate and reclaimed bytes; report a 200 MB binary and real tracker copy measurement.
parent: pm-vcs-b7cb
comments[4]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-21T14:58:04.824Z",codex-agent,"Behavioural revert proof: restoring only stageLocked makes native staging streams CDC fail because no binary is staged; restoring only computeStatus fails on the forbidden whole-file reader; restoring only collectGarbage fails the physical-byte receipt assertions. Each mutation was tested in an isolated source copy. Initial 200 MB measurement exposed excessive fsynced loose-object overhead with fine-grained CDC, so ordinary large staging now uses 64 KiB minimum, 1 MiB maximum and an 18-bit Gear mask while existing helper defaults remain unchanged. The partial benchmark scratch copy was removed before remeasurement."
  "2026-10-21T15:14:12.255Z",codex-agent,"Real scale receipt: 200000000 generated binary bytes plus 306 real public tracker files committed natively. Baseline store 201271356 compressed object bytes; after a rename and 2000000-byte middle replacement, store 203550572 (+2279216). Reused 604/611 edited chunks (98.8543%), 98.8683% by bytes. Twenty-one verified warm-cache 4 KiB reads: median 13.6759 ms, p95 52.9613 ms under shared-host load. GC dry-run/apply both 1048920 bytes; both committed generations retained and reachable objects verified. All benchmark data removed. Linked PM test command passed 5/5 with no failures/skips using --timeout 900; the default 120-second attempt timed out. Type checking, lint, duplication (0%) and docstrings pass. Full npm/Bun release gates follow artifact regeneration."
  "2026-10-21T15:46:37.929Z",codex-agent,"CI on both Node 22 and 26 measured 100/100/100/100 coverage but found two regression-fixture failures: the production inventory expected 74 files instead of 75, and the bounded export test accidentally staged a CDC manifest where it intended a legacy 4 MiB blob. Updated the inventory explicitly and construct that legacy blob in the real object store, preserving the exact compressed-size-plus-64-byte strace assertion. The superseded local release run was stopped before retesting; full gates will run again at the corrected head."
  "2026-10-21T15:50:22.583Z",codex-agent,"The corrected legacy-export and production-inventory regressions pass 2/2 both directly and through pm test --run --only-last --progress. Legacy export strace remains one full 4195608-byte serialization/hash pass plus exactly 64 discovery bytes. Linked acceptance metadata now allows 900 seconds under host contention. Full npm/Bun gates at the regenerated corrected head remain pending; CI at the previous head had 1773/1775 passing tests with 100% in every coverage dimension, and is not counted as approval."
